## Step 9 — Generate the HTML report
 
Write a single self-contained `.html` file to the output path. No external
dependencies — all images are base64 inline, all styles are in a `<style>` block.
 
### Page structure
 
```
<header>
  Figma ↔ Code Audit
  File: [name]   Node: [id]   Generated: [date]
</header>
 
<summary-bar>
  ✅ N  🟠 N  🟡 N  🔴 N  ⚪ N
</summary-bar>
 
[for each matched component]
<component-card>
  <card-header>
    ComponentName        <pill>N issues</pill>
  </card-header>
  <panels>
    <panel label="Figma">
      <img src="data:image/png;base64,..." />
    </panel>
    <panel label="Code">
      [inline HTML preview from Step 8]
    </panel>
  </panels>
  <diff-table>
    property | Figma value (token) | Code value (token) | ✅/🟠/🟡/🔴/⚪
  </diff-table>
</component-card>
 
[missing components section — red cards, one panel only]
[unused tokens section — grey table]
```
 
### Styling rules
 
- Page background: `#f5f5f5`; max content width `1200px`, centered
- Component cards: white, `border-radius: 8px`, `box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,.08)`, `margin-bottom: 24px`
- Panel label ("Figma" / "Code"): uppercase, `font-size: 11px`, `letter-spacing: .05em`, `color: #6b7280`; panel background `#f9fafb`; both panels equal width, `min-height: 120px`, content centered
- Diff table rows colour-coded:
  - ✅ `background: #f0fdf4`
  - 🟠 `background: #fff7ed; border-left: 3px solid #f97316`
  - 🟡 `background: #fefce8; border-left: 3px solid #eab308`
  - 🔴 `background: #fef2f2; border-left: 3px solid #ef4444`
  - ⚪ `background: #f9fafb`
- Issue badge on card header: small pill, `background: #f97316; color: white` if any
  🟠/🟡, `background: #ef4444` if any 🔴, hidden if all ✅
- Missing component cards: full-width, red-tinted header, left panel shows Figma
  screenshot or extracted spec, right panel shows a grey "Not implemented in code"
  placeholder box
### Callout badges on previews
 
Where a property is flagged 🟠 or 🔴, add a small floating badge on the affected
preview panel to draw the eye to the specific discrepancy. Wrap the preview in
`position: relative` and add `position: absolute` badges (e.g. `"height ≠"`,
`"border ≠"`) near the relevant area. Keep badges visually small and use the same
orange/red colour as the diff table rows.
 
